Description:

Rolling replication splits large mailbox updates into batches of
sync_batchsize records, oldest changes first.  This now covers flag and
annotation changes as well as appends, and works again: since 3.4 the
batching setting never reached the code that applied it.  Large bulk
changes no longer have to be held in memory all at once by sync_client
and sync_server.


Documentation:

sync_batchsize in imapd.conf(5).


Config changes:

sync_batchsize


Upgrade instructions:

None.  A replica receiving a partial batch needs no new support.


GitHub issue:

None.
